{
  $schema: 'https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json',
  // NOTE: all rules below use automergeType:'pr' (+ platformAutomerge:true in
  // renovate.json5), NOT 'branch'. The flux-local gate runs `on: pull_request`
  // only, so it never runs on a bare branch — with 'branch' Renovate could never
  // see a green branch, fell back to opening a PR, and then (in branch mode) never
  // merged it, so every eligible PR sat green forever (e.g. #1816). 'pr' +
  // platformAutomerge hands the merge to GitHub, which fires when flux-local passes
  // — independent of Mend's hosted run cadence — and leaves a visible merged-PR trail.
  packageRules: [
    // ── minimumReleaseAge REMOVED 2026-07-18 (GHCR bake freeze) ────────────────
    // The Tier-2 rules used to carry a 3-day `minimumReleaseAge` soak. Mend-hosted
    // Renovate cannot obtain a release timestamp for the `docker` datasource on
    // ghcr.io (multi-arch OCI images), so with internalChecksFilter:strict (default)
    // the internal stability check NEVER passed for GHCR images — every GHCR Tier-2
    // update sat in the dependency dashboard's "Pending Status Checks" with no
    // branch/PR, indefinitely and silently, since ~2026-07-06. Docker Hub images
    // (ollama/wyoming/mcp-grafana) were unaffected (timestamp readable), which is why
    // "some merged, most didn't". Removing the soak restores hands-off GHCR
    // auto-merge; the 3-day bake's safety is redundant with the flux-local gate +
    // shepherd + health gate + auto-revert. If GHCR timestamp lookups are ever fixed
    // host-side (a ghcr.io hostRules token on the Renovate runner), a bake can be
    // reintroduced. See issue #1809 + memory renovate-automation-roadmap.
    // ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Tier 0 — github-actions, ALL update types incl. major (widened 2026-07-08).
    // GHA bumps are trivially revertible (revert the workflow file) and, crucially,
    // FAIL-SAFE: with ignoreTests:false a major that breaks a workflow turns that
    // workflow's required check RED on its own PR, so it never auto-merges — it
    // strands (correctly) instead of merging broken. Even a major to a SAFETY-GATE
    // workflow (flux-local / diff-scope) can only make its check red, which halts
    // all auto-merge (fail-closed), never waves something bad through. So there is no
    // "the gate auto-merged a break in itself" hole. This is the revertible-vs-one-way
    // principle applied to CI: revertible + self-gating => hands-off.
    {
      description: 'Auto merge GitHub Actions (incl. majors — gated + fail-safe)',
      matchManagers: ['github-actions'],
      matchUpdateTypes: ['major', 'minor', 'patch', 'digest'],
      automerge: true,
      automergeType: 'pr',
      ignoreTests: false,
    },
    // Tier 2 — our own images. We build and test these before pushing, so a
    // Renovate digest/tag bump is a no-brainer (no soak — bake removed, see header).
    {
      description: 'Auto merge our own ghcr.io/thaynes43/* images',
      matchDatasources: ['docker'],
      matchPackageNames: ['/thaynes43//'],
      matchUpdateTypes: ['minor', 'patch', 'digest'],
      automerge: true,
      automergeType: 'pr',
      ignoreTests: false,
    },
    // Tier 2 — kube-prometheus-stack chart (observability has been quiet here).
    // Sourced via OCIRepository (oci://ghcr.io/.../charts/kube-prometheus-stack),
    // which Renovate tracks as the `docker` datasource — not `helm`. Match both
    // so it works whether the chart is OCI- or HelmRepository-sourced.
    {
      description: 'Auto merge kube-prometheus-stack minor/patch',
      matchDatasources: ['docker', 'helm'],
      matchPackageNames: ['/kube-prometheus-stack/'],
      matchUpdateTypes: ['minor', 'patch'],
      automerge: true,
      automergeType: 'pr',
      ignoreTests: false,
    },
    // Tier 2 — safe stateless leaf-app domains on the main cluster. These apps
    // restart as a single pod with no operator/coupling/state-migration risk.
    // Gated by flux-local (3-day bake removed 2026-07-18, see header). Ramp as each proves quiet.
    //
    // observability/ added 2026-06-15: the whole domain is plain Deployments
    // (no StatefulSets, no operator CRs) — grafana's state lives in external
    // CNPG (durable), loki's only PVC is local log storage (a bad upgrade
    // loses logs, not the cluster). kube-prometheus-stack is already trusted
    // by name above. Accepted trade-off: observability IS the safety net that
    // watches the other Tier 2 merges, so a bad monitoring push could blind
    // us — mitigated by the flux-local gate, the 3-day bake, and the
    // Gatus/Pushover/watchdog alert path that does NOT depend on Prometheus.
    // Watch item: prometheus-operator-crds (CRD-only bumps) — safe here only
    // because minor/patch CRD changes are additive; majors stay manual.
    // Edge (2026-07-05): the `kubernetes/*/apps/…` glob (the `*` matches ONE
    // segment) covers BOTH `main` and `edge`. Decision: edge PRs auto-merge on
    // the SAME safe-leaf policy as main. Rationale: flux-local fully renders the
    // edge cluster in its matrix on these (main-targeted) PRs and Diff Scope
    // runs, so edge gets the same render + scope gates; we just can't RUNTIME-
    // validate edge (it is powered off) and that is accepted — nothing runs
    // there to break. Cluster-killers (cilium, coredns, flux) stay OFF this list
    // for BOTH clusters, so a bad push can't wedge edge when it is next booted.
    {
      description: 'Auto merge safe leaf-app domains (stateless, single-pod) — main + edge',
      matchFileNames: [
        'kubernetes/*/apps/media/**',
        'kubernetes/*/apps/ai/**',
        'kubernetes/*/apps/downloads/**',
        'kubernetes/*/apps/frontend/**',
        'kubernetes/*/apps/office/**',
        'kubernetes/*/apps/photos/**',
        'kubernetes/*/apps/observability/**',
        // home-automation added 2026-07-05 (hands-off directive: only cluster-breakers
        // stay manual). All leaf apps — HA, esphome, z2m, zwave, music-assistant,
        // appdaemon, go2rtc, ha-mcp, music-assistant — plain Deployments, no operator/
        // CRD/StatefulSet. HA + z2m are the highest-blast members (a bad bump degrades
        // the smart home, not the cluster); the flux-local gate + the HA watchdogs +
        // nightly HA backups are the safety net. appdaemon is ghcr.io/thaynes43/* (also
        // Tier-2 by the "our own images" rule).
        'kubernetes/*/apps/home-automation/**',
      ],
      // 'digest' (2026-06-28): SHA-pinned image refreshes on the SAME tag are at
      // least as safe as minor/patch for these stateless single-pod apps, yet the
      // minor/patch-only list stranded every digest bump forever (cloudflare-ddns
      // #1884, postgres-init #1889/#1890). The Immich carve-out below still blocks
      // immich-app/* digests (matches by package name, last rule wins per-dep).
      matchUpdateTypes: ['minor', 'patch', 'digest'],
      automerge: true,
      automergeType: 'pr',
      ignoreTests: false,
    },
    // Tier 2 (2026-06-15) — curated cluster-infra leaves, allowlisted by
    // EXPLICIT SUBPATH (never whole-domain). kube-system and network each
    // contain a cluster-killer that GitOps can't self-heal if a bad push lands
    // overnight — cilium/coredns (CNI + cluster DNS), traefik (all ingress),
    // authentik (SSO + DB migrations), multus (CNI), the device-plugins
    // (GPU/detection pipeline). Only stateless, single-pod utilities with no
    // such coupling go here. Same flux-local gate (bake removed, see header). Ramp per-app.
    // `kubernetes/*/apps/…` again covers main + edge (see the leaf-app note above).
    // Edge currently has metrics-server, reloader, spegel of these; the rest match
    // main only (harmless — no edge dir to match). cilium/coredns on edge are
    // deliberately NOT here (cluster-killers, stay manual on both clusters).
    {
      description: 'Auto merge safe cluster-infra leaves (explicit subpaths) — main + edge',
      matchFileNames: [
        'kubernetes/*/apps/kube-system/metrics-server/**',
        'kubernetes/*/apps/kube-system/reloader/**',
        'kubernetes/*/apps/kube-system/reflector/**',
        'kubernetes/*/apps/kube-system/k8tz/**',
        'kubernetes/*/apps/kube-system/spegel/**',
        'kubernetes/*/apps/network/cloudflare-ddns/**',
        // cloudflare-tunnel (2026-07-10): same class as cloudflare-ddns — a stateless
        // app-template Deployment (cloudflared). Revertible + the bot can auto-revert
        // it (not in the diff-scope-blocked trees), and a tunnel break is Gatus-visible
        // + LAN/internal-unaffected. Was stranded only because it wasn't listed here.
        'kubernetes/*/apps/network/cloudflare-tunnel/**',
      ],
      // 'digest' included for the same reason as the leaf-app rule above.
      matchUpdateTypes: ['minor', 'patch', 'digest'],
      automerge: true,
      automergeType: 'pr',
      ignoreTests: false,
    },
    // qBittorrent carve-out (2026-07-11) — MAM approved-clients compliance. MyAnonaMouse
    // requires the torrent client to be on its Approved Clients list with auto-update
    // DISABLED; an unattended merge could deploy a version MAM hasn't approved yet and
    // risk the account. The bump PR still opens — the owner checks the new version
    // against MAM's approved-clients page, then merges by hand. Matches by package name
    // so it beats the downloads/** leaf rule above (last rule wins per-dep). See
    // haynesnetwork .agents/plans/031-books-acquisition-mam.md + the MAM rules scrape.
    {
      description: 'NEVER auto-merge qbittorrent — MAM approved-clients compliance (manual merge only)',
      matchDatasources: ['docker'],
      matchPackageNames: ['/home-operations/qbittorrent$/'],
      automerge: false,
    },
    // Plex — Renovate NEVER auto-merges it; the upgrade-shepherd OWNS it (2026-07-19).
    // Why: a Plex pod restart DURING a Kometa run corrupts Kometa's in-flight library
    // write, so the merge must be TIMED. `automerge:false` keeps Renovate's hands off;
    // plex is in the shepherd RAMP (UPGRADE_AGENT_RAMP), which runs a KOMETA-IDLE
    // PREFLIGHT before enabling auto-merge and holds to its next 4h run if a Kometa job
    // is running or imminent. Matches by package name so it beats the media/** leaf rule
    // (last rule wins per-dep). See the shepherd prompt PLEX clause +
    // .agents/runbooks/tier4-component-playbooks.md; memory opsplex-launch-gotchas.
    {
      description: 'plex — Renovate never auto-merges; upgrade-shepherd owns it (Kometa-idle preflight)',
      matchDatasources: ['docker'],
      matchPackageNames: ['/home-operations/plex$/'],
      automerge: false,
    },
    // Immich carve-out REMOVED 2026-07-05 (hands-off directive). Immich minor/patch/
    // digest now auto-merge via the photos leaf-app rule above — it is not cluster-
    // breaking, and the safety net (flux-local + health gate + auto-revert + the daily
    // postgres16-pgvecto backup + the CNPG backup-failure alerts) covers a bad minor
    // migration. Immich MAJORS still never auto-merge here (the leaf rule is minor/
    // patch/digest only) — the upgrade-shepherd owns immich majors (reads the release
    // notes, backup-gates, and auto-merges a pure major or authors a supporting-edit PR
    // for review). See kubernetes/main/apps/upgrade-agent/shepherd + docs/renovate/README.md.
  ],
}
